{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E7bXXsGdtwmk4WJ8c4n9xK","type":"tool_result","content":"# offline replica, data as of 2026-05-01T00:00:00Z\nid:\t808bc6785589a2f7f1be1aa5\nlist:\tdev@kafka.apache.org\nfrom:\tKirk True (Jira)\ndate:\t2026-04-23T17:54:00Z\nsubject:\t[jira] [Created] (KAFKA-20525) Support client configuration observability\nthread:\tJIRA.13648992.1776966822000@Atlassian.JIRA\nin-reply-to:\tJIRA.13648992.1776966822000@Atlassian.JIRA\n\nKirk True created KAFKA-20525:\n---------------------------------\n\n             Summary: Support client configuration observability\n                 Key: KAFKA-20525\n                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20525\n             Project: Kafka\n          Issue Type: New Feature\n          Components: clients\n            Reporter: Kirk True\n            Assignee: Kirk True\n\n\nThis KIP adds a new RPC to the Kafka protocol that forms a _handshake_ between the client and broker, named {{{}PushConfig{}}}, by which the client sends the configuration (keys and values) to the broker. Brokers interact with a new {{ClientConfigPolicy}} interface to process the above RPCs from the client.\n\nSee [KIP-1324.|https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1324%3A+Support+client+configuration+observability]\nh2.\n\n\n\n--\nThis message was sent by Atlassian Jira\n(v8.20.10#820010)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b94b9368-2542-4780-96d0-6b5a0d729b3f","uuid":"af0404a3-8684-475f-afa8-59480419dd9f","timestamp":"2026-09-27T16:35:18.388Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# offline replica, data as of 2026-05-01T00:00:00Z\nid:\t808bc6785589a2f7f1be1aa5\nlist:\tdev@kafka.apache.org\nfrom:\tKirk True (Jira)\ndate:\t2026-04-23T17:54:00Z\nsubject:\t[jira] [Created] (KAFKA-20525) Support client configuration observability\nthread:\tJIRA.13648992.1776966822000@Atlassian.JIRA\nin-reply-to:\tJIRA.13648992.1776966822000@Atlassian.JIRA\n\nKirk True created KAFKA-20525:\n---------------------------------\n\n             Summary: Support client configuration observability\n                 Key: KAFKA-20525\n                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20525\n             Project: Kafka\n          Issue Type: New Feature\n          Components: clients\n            Reporter: Kirk True\n            Assignee: Kirk True\n\n\nThis KIP adds a new RPC to the Kafka protocol that forms a _handshake_ between the client and broker, named {{{}PushConfig{}}}, by which the client sends the configuration (keys and values) to the broker. Brokers interact with a new {{ClientConfigPolicy}} interface to process the above RPCs from the client.\n\nSee [KIP-1324.|https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1324%3A+Support+client+configuration+observability]\nh2.\n\n\n\n--\nThis message was sent by Atlassian Jira\n(v8.20.10#820010)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
